---
title: Brie and blueberry gelato
category: Desserts
course: Desserts
tags:
  - Italy
  - ice cream
  - gelato
cuisine: Italian
servings: 8
difficulty: medium
cook time: 45 minutes
prep time: 7 hours
created: 2026-07-29
updated: 2026-07-29
---

In a pan, mix together @whole milk{550%g}, @fresh cream{200%g}(35% fat), and @powdered skim milk{40%g}.

Add @sugar{90%g}, @glucose syrup{45%g}(45 DE), @honey{15%g}, and @fine table salt{1%g}.

Turn on the heat and bring the mixture to 40°C, then add @egg yolks{4} and allow it to rise to 85°C. At this point add @carob flour{3%g}. The temperature will both pasteurise the mixture and activate the carob flour.

Turn off the heat and add @Brie{150%g}(diced, no rind).

Blend with an #immersion blender{} until smooth.

Leave the mixture to refrigerate at 4°C for ~{4-6%hours} (ideally overnight).

In the meantime, wash, thoroughly dry, and freeze @blueberries{100%g}.

Pour the chilled mixture into an #ice cream maker{} and churn until creamy, about ~{20-30%minutes}. Toss in the frozen blueberries within the last 5 minutes of the churning process.

Pour out the gelato into a wide plastic container with a lid and freeze at -18°C for ~{3-4%hours}.

After this time it should still be soft enough to scoop. If frozen for longer periods, let it sit at room temperature for about ~{10%minutes} before serving.